IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa27-definitions`
IMPORT `coa27-ch4-register`

-- coa27-ch6-administration.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 42 Chapter 6 (part): ss 1251 (fees), 1251A (report on
-- inspections), 1252 and 1253 (delegation of the Secretary of State's functions), 1254 (international obligations) and
-- ss 1258, 1259 (service of notices), lines 17699-17756, 17867-17882 and 17909-17937 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively); part agent coa27.
--
-- WHAT IS NOT HERE. Powers to make regulations or orders are machinery, inert in the coverage table (reason 2): s 1251(2) and (4),
-- s 1252(1), (5), (8) to (12), s 1253(1) and (4). The consequential-amendments pointer s 1264 and the power in s 1263 likewise.
-- READING A RESULT (the rule of 2026-10-29): JUST TRUE the text says yes; JUST FALSE the text says no in its own words
-- ("unless", "if", "except", "only if", "other than"); NOTHING the text does not decide. A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every name begins with the section label it implements.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1251 Fees
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17701 | (1) An applicant for a recognition order under this Part must pay such fee in respect of his application as the Secretary of State may by regulations prescribe; and no application is to be regarded as duly made unless this subsection is complied with.
@ref s 1251(1) Fees: the application fee (src:17701-17701)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant for a recognition order under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee the Secretary of State has prescribed by regulations, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 1251(1) the fee the applicant must pay in pounds` MEANS
    IF `the person is an applicant for a recognition order under this Part`
    THEN JUST `the fee the Secretary of State has prescribed by regulations, in pounds`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An applicant for a recognition order under this Part must pay such fee"

@ref s 1251(1) Fees: when an application is duly made (src:17701-17701)
GIVEN `the fee in respect of the application has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1251(1) the application is duly made` MEANS
    IF `the fee in respect of the application has been paid`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paying the fee is necessary and the text does not say it is enough
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no application is to be regarded as duly made unless this subsection is complied with"

-- src:17707 | (3) Fees received by the Secretary of State by virtue of this Part are to be paid into the Consolidated Fund.
@ref s 1251(3) Fees: the Consolidated Fund (src:17707-17707)
GIVEN `the fees were received by the Secretary of State by virtue of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1251(3) the fees are to be paid into the Consolidated Fund` MEANS
    IF `the fees were received by the Secretary of State by virtue of this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Fees received by the Secretary of State by virtue of this Part"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1251A Duty of the Secretary of State to report on inspections
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17711 | The Secretary of State must, at least once in every calendar year, publish a report containing a summary of the results of inspections that are delivered to him—
-- src:17712 | (a) by the Independent Supervisor under section 1229(5A);
-- src:17713 | (b) by a recognised supervisory body under paragraph 13(12) of Schedule 10.
@ref s 1251A Report on inspections: at least once in every calendar year (src:17711-17713)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the days on which the Secretary of State published a report containing a summary of the results of inspections delivered to him by the Independent Supervisor under section 1229(5A) or by a recognised supervisory body under paragraph 13(12) of Schedule 10` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1251A the Secretary of State has published the report required for the calendar year` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN d YIELD DATE_YEAR d EQUALS year)
           `the days on which the Secretary of State published a report containing a summary of the results of inspections delivered to him by the Independent Supervisor under section 1229(5A) or by a recognised supervisory body under paragraph 13(12) of Schedule 10`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, at least once in every calendar year, publish a report" (a period fixed in the text's own words: the ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)); a year with no report is one in which the duty was not met

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1252 Delegation of the Secretary of State's functions
-- =========================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 1252(2) kind of body` IS ONE OF
    `s 1252(2)(a) a body corporate established by the order`
    `s 1252(2)(b) an existing body`
    `s 1252(2) some other body`

-- src:17717 | (2) The body designated by a delegation order may be either—
-- src:17718 | (a) a body corporate which is established by the order, or
-- src:17719 | (b) subject to section 1253, a body (including the competent authority, and whether a body corporate or an unincorporated association) which is already in existence (“an existing body”).
@ref s 1252(2) Delegation: the body designated (src:17717-17719)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1252(2) kind of body`
      `section 1253 allows the existing body to be designated` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1252(2) the body may be designated by a delegation order` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 1252(2)(a) a body corporate established by the order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1252(2)(b) an existing body` THEN `section 1253 allows the existing body to be designated`
        -- subject to section 1253, whose answer is an input: NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when that answer is NOTHING
    WHEN `s 1252(2) some other body` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The body designated by a delegation order may be either— (a) ... or (b)"

-- src:17720 | (3) A delegation order has the effect of making the body designated by the order designated under section 5 of the Freedom of Information Act 2000 (c. 36) (further powers to designate public authorities).
@ref s 1252(3) Delegation: the Freedom of Information Act 2000 (src:17720-17720)
GIVEN `the body is designated by a delegation order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1252(3) the body is designated under section 5 of the Freedom of Information Act 2000` MEANS
    IF `the body is designated by a delegation order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A delegation order has the effect of making the body designated by the order designated"

-- The functions that subsections (4), (6) and (7) distinguish.
DECLARE `s 1252(4) function of the Secretary of State` IS ONE OF
    `s 1252(4)(b)(i) a function in relation to the body itself`
    `s 1252(4)(b)(ii) a function under section 1228 (appointment of Independent Supervisor)`
    `s 1252(6)(a) a function under section 1224 (power to call for information from recognised bodies etc)`
    `s 1252(6)(b) a function under section 1244 (power to call for information from registered third country auditors)`
    `s 1252(6)(c) a function under section 1254 (directions to comply with international obligations)`
    `s 1252(7)(a) the function of refusing to make a declaration under section 1221(1) on the grounds referred to in section 1221(4)`
    `s 1252(7)(b) the function of withdrawing a declaration under section 1221(7) on those grounds`
    `s 1252(4) another function under this Part`

-- src:17721 | (4) A delegation order has the effect of transferring to the body designated by it all functions of the Secretary of State under this Part—
-- src:17722 | (a) subject to such exceptions and reservations as may be specified in the order, and
-- src:17723 | (b) except—
-- src:17724 | (i) his functions in relation to the body itself, and
-- src:17725 | (ii) his functions under section 1228 (appointment of Independent Supervisor).
@ref s 1252(4) Delegation: what is transferred (src:17721-17725)
GIVEN f IS A `s 1252(4) function of the Secretary of State`
      `the delegation order specifies an exception for the function` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1252(4) the function is transferred to the designated body` MEANS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `s 1252(4)(b)(i) a function in relation to the body itself` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except— (i) his functions in relation to the body itself"
    WHEN `s 1252(4)(b)(ii) a function under section 1228 (appointment of Independent Supervisor)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except ... (ii) his functions under section 1228"
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the delegation order specifies an exception for the function`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subject to such exceptions and reservations as may be specified in the order"
        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:17727 | (6) Any transfer of functions under the following provisions must be subject to the reservation that the functions remain exercisable concurrently by the Secretary of State—
-- src:17728 | (a) section 1224 (power to call for information from recognised bodies etc);
-- src:17729 | (b) section 1244 (power to call for information from registered third country auditors);
-- src:17730 | (c) section 1254 (directions to comply with international obligations).
@ref s 1252(6) Delegation: concurrent exercise (src:17727-17730)
GIVEN f IS A `s 1252(4) function of the Secretary of State`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1252(6) the transfer is subject to the reservation that the function remains exercisable concurrently by the Secretary of State` MEANS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `s 1252(6)(a) a function under section 1224 (power to call for information from recognised bodies etc)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1252(6)(b) a function under section 1244 (power to call for information from registered third country auditors)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1252(6)(c) a function under section 1254 (directions to comply with international obligations)` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any transfer of functions under the following provisions"

-- src:17731 | (7) Any transfer of—
-- src:17732 | (a) the function of refusing to make a declaration under section 1221(1) (approval of third country qualifications) on the grounds referred to in section 1221(4) (lack of comparable treatment), or
-- src:17733 | (b) the function of withdrawing such a declaration under section 1221(7) on those grounds,
-- src:17734 | must be subject to the reservation that the function is exercisable only with the consent of the Secretary of State.
@ref s 1252(7) Delegation: functions exercisable only with consent (src:17731-17734)
GIVEN f IS A `s 1252(4) function of the Secretary of State`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1252(7) the transfer is subject to the reservation that the function is exercisable only with the consent of the Secretary of State` MEANS
    CONSIDER f
    WHEN `s 1252(7)(a) the function of refusing to make a declaration under section 1221(1) on the grounds referred to in section 1221(4)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1252(7)(b) the function of withdrawing a declaration under section 1221(7) on those grounds` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any transfer of— (a) the function of refusing ... (b) the function of withdrawing"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1253 Delegation of functions to an existing body
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17749 | (3) The conditions are—
-- src:17750 | (a) that the functions in question will be exercised effectively, and
-- src:17751 | (b) where the delegation order is to contain any requirements or other provisions specified under subsection (4), that those functions will be exercised in accordance with any such requirements or provisions.
@ref s 1253(3) Delegation to an existing body: the conditions (src:17749-17751)
GIVEN `the functions in question will be exercised effectively` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the delegation order is to contain requirements or other provisions specified under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those functions will be exercised in accordance with any such requirements or provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253(3) the conditions are met` MEANS
    IF       `the functions in question will be exercised effectively`
         AND (IF `the delegation order is to contain requirements or other provisions specified under subsection (4)`
              THEN `those functions will be exercised in accordance with any such requirements or provisions`
              ELSE TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are— (a) ... and (b)"

-- src:17746 | (2) The Secretary of State may make such a delegation order if it appears to him that—
-- src:17747 | (a) the body is able and willing to exercise the functions that would be transferred by the order, and
-- src:17748 | (b) the body has arrangements in place relating to the exercise of those functions which are such as to be likely to ensure that the conditions in subsection (3) are met.
@ref s 1253(2) Delegation to an existing body: when the order may be made (src:17746-17748)
GIVEN `it appears to the Secretary of State that the body is able and willing to exercise the functions that would be transferred by the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to him that the body has arrangements in place relating to the exercise of those functions which are such as to be likely to ensure that the conditions in subsection (3) are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253(2) the Secretary of State may make the delegation order designating the existing body` MEANS
    IF       `it appears to the Secretary of State that the body is able and willing to exercise the functions that would be transferred by the order`
         AND `it appears to him that the body has arrangements in place relating to the exercise of those functions which are such as to be likely to ensure that the conditions in subsection (3) are met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Secretary of State may make such a delegation order if it appears to him that" (name test of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q3)

-- src:17753 | (5) An existing body—
-- src:17754 | (a) may be designated by a delegation order under section 1252, and
-- src:17755 | (b) may accordingly exercise functions of the Secretary of State in pursuance of the order,
-- src:17756 | despite any involvement of the body in the exercise of any functions under arrangements within ... paragraph 1 or 2 of Schedule 12.
@ref s 1253(5) Delegation to an existing body: involvement in Schedule 12 arrangements (src:17753-17756)
GIVEN `the existing body is involved in the exercise of functions under arrangements within paragraph 1 or 2 of Schedule 12` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1253(5) the existing body may be designated and may exercise the functions despite its involvement` MEANS
    IF `the existing body is involved in the exercise of functions under arrangements within paragraph 1 or 2 of Schedule 12`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "despite any involvement of the body"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1254 Directions to comply with international obligations
-- =========================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 1254(1) kind of body` IS ONE OF
    `s 1254(1)(a)(i) a recognised supervisory body`
    `s 1254(1)(a)(ii) a recognised qualifying body`
    `s 1254(1)(a)(iii) a person keeping a register of auditors, or part of such a register, in accordance with regulations under section 1239(1)`
    `s 1254(1)(a)(iv) a body exercising functions under arrangements within Schedule 12`
    `s 1254(1)(a)(v) the Independent Supervisor`
    `s 1254(1)(a)(vi) the competent authority`
    `s 1254(1)(a)(vii) a body designated by order under section 1252`
    `s 1254(1) another body`

-- src:17869 | (1) If it appears to the Secretary of State—
-- src:17870 | (a) that any action proposed to be taken by—
-- src:17871 | (i) a recognised supervisory body,
-- src:17872 | (ii) a recognised qualifying body,
-- src:17873 | (iii) a person keeping a register of auditors, or part of such a register, in accordance with regulations under section 1239(1),
-- src:17874 | (iv) a body exercising functions under arrangements within Schedule 12,
-- src:17875 | (v) the Independent Supervisor,
-- src:17876 | (vi) the competent authority, or
-- src:17877 | (vii) a body designated by order under section 1252,
-- src:17878 | would be incompatible with assimilated obligations or any other international obligations of the United Kingdom, or
-- src:17879 | (b) that any action which that body has power to take is required for the purpose of implementing any such obligations,
-- src:17880 | he may direct the body not to take or, as the case may be, to take the action in question.
@ref s 1254(1) International obligations: the direction (src:17869-17880)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1254(1) kind of body`
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that action proposed to be taken by the body would be incompatible with assimilated obligations or any other international obligations of the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that action which the body has power to take is required for the purpose of implementing any such obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1254(1) the Secretary of State may direct the body not to take or to take the action` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 1254(1) another body` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the direction may be given to the bodies named in (a)(i) to (vii)
    OTHERWISE
        IF       `it appears to the Secretary of State that action proposed to be taken by the body would be incompatible with assimilated obligations or any other international obligations of the United Kingdom`
              OR `it appears to the Secretary of State that action which the body has power to take is required for the purpose of implementing any such obligations`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If it appears to the Secretary of State— (a) ... or (b) ... he may direct" (name test of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q4)

-- src:17881 | (2) A direction may include such supplementary or incidental requirements as the Secretary of State thinks necessary or expedient.
@ref s 1254(2) International obligations: supplementary requirements (src:17881-17881)
GIVEN `the requirement is supplementary or incidental and the Secretary of State thinks it necessary or expedient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1254(2) the direction may include the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the requirement is supplementary or incidental and the Secretary of State thinks it necessary or expedient`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such supplementary or incidental requirements as the Secretary of State thinks necessary or expedient"

-- src:17882 | (3) A direction under this section given to the Independent Supervisor , the competent authority or a body designated by order under section 1252 is enforceable on the application of the Secretary of State by injunction or, in Scotland, by an order under section 45 of the Court of Session Act 1988 (c. 36).
@ref s 1254(3) International obligations: enforcement (src:17882-17882)
GIVEN `the direction is given to the Independent Supervisor, the competent authority or a body designated by order under section 1252` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 1239(8) remedy`
`s 1254(3) the direction is enforceable by` MEANS
    IF `the direction is given to the Independent Supervisor, the competent authority or a body designated by order under section 1252` AND `the Secretary of State has applied`
    THEN
        IF `the proceedings are in Scotland`
        THEN JUST `s 1239(8) an order under section 45 of the Court of Session Act 1988`
        ELSE JUST `s 1239(8) an injunction`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A direction under this section given to the Independent Supervisor, the competent authority or a body designated by order under section 1252 is enforceable on the application of the Secretary of State"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1258 Service of notices
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17911 | (1) This section has effect in relation to any notice, direction or other document required or authorised by or by virtue of this Part to be given to or served on any person other than the Secretary of State.
@ref s 1258(1) Service of notices: scope (src:17911-17911)
GIVEN `the document is a notice, direction or other document required or authorised by or by virtue of this Part to be given to or served on a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1258(1) this section has effect in relation to the document` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document is a notice, direction or other document required or authorised by or by virtue of this Part to be given to or served on a person`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any notice, direction or other document required or authorised by or by virtue of this Part"
    ELSE IF `the person is the Secretary of State`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to be given to or served on any person other than the Secretary of State"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 1258(2) method` IS ONE OF
    `s 1258(2)(a) delivering it to him`
    `s 1258(2)(b) leaving it at his proper address`
    `s 1258(2)(c) sending it by post to him at that address`
    `s 1258(2) another method`

-- src:17912 | (2) Any such document may be given to or served on the person in question—
-- src:17913 | (a) by delivering it to him,
-- src:17914 | (b) by leaving it at his proper address, or
-- src:17915 | (c) by sending it by post to him at that address.
@ref s 1258(2) Service of notices: the methods (src:17912-17915)
GIVEN method IS A `s 1258(2) method`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1258(2) the document may be given to or served on the person by the method` MEANS
    CONSIDER method
    WHEN `s 1258(2)(a) delivering it to him` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1258(2)(b) leaving it at his proper address` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1258(2)(c) sending it by post to him at that address` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 1258(2) another method` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the three methods are not said to be the only ones (section 1259 adds electronic transmission)

DECLARE `s 1258(3) kind of recipient` IS ONE OF
    `s 1258(3)(a) a body corporate`
    `s 1258(3)(b) a partnership`
    `s 1258(3)(c) an unincorporated association other than a partnership`

-- src:17916 | (3) Any such document may—
-- src:17917 | (a) in the case of a body corporate, be given to or served on an officer of that body;
-- src:17918 | (b) in the case of a partnership, be given to or served on any partner;
-- src:17919 | (c) in the case of an unincorporated association other than a partnership, be given to or served on any member of the governing body of that association.
@ref s 1258(3) Service of notices: service on an officer, partner or member (src:17916-17919)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1258(3) kind of recipient`
      `the person served is an officer of the body corporate, any partner, or any member of the governing body of the association (as the kind of recipient requires)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1258(3) service on the person is service on the recipient` MEANS
    IF `the person served is an officer of the body corporate, any partner, or any member of the governing body of the association (as the kind of recipient requires)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, in the case of a body corporate, be given to or served on an officer of that body" (a permission, not said to be the only way)

-- src:17920 | (4) For the purposes of this section and section 7 of the Interpretation Act 1978 (c. 30) (service of documents by post) in its application to this section, the proper address of any person is his last known address (whether of his residence or of a place where he carries on business or is employed) and also—
-- src:17921 | (a) in the case of a person who is eligible under the rules of a recognised supervisory body for appointment as a statutory auditor and who does not have a place of business in the United Kingdom, the address of that body;
-- src:17922 | (b) in the case of a body corporate or an officer of that body, the address of the registered or principal office of that body in the United Kingdom;
-- src:17923 | (c) in the case of an unincorporated association other than a partnership or a member of its governing body, its principal office in the United Kingdom.
@ref s 1258(4) Service of notices: the proper address (src:17920-17923)
GIVEN `the address is the person's last known address (whether of his residence or of a place where he carries on business or is employed)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is eligible under the rules of a recognised supervisory body for appointment as a statutory auditor, has no place of business in the United Kingdom, and the address is that of that body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a body corporate or an officer of that body, and the address is that of the registered or principal office of that body in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an unincorporated association other than a partnership or a member of its governing body, and the address is its principal office in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1258(4) the address is a proper address of the person` MEANS
    IF       `the address is the person's last known address (whether of his residence or of a place where he carries on business or is employed)`
          OR `the person is eligible under the rules of a recognised supervisory body for appointment as a statutory auditor, has no place of business in the United Kingdom, and the address is that of that body`
          OR `the person is a body corporate or an officer of that body, and the address is that of the registered or principal office of that body in the United Kingdom`
          OR `the person is an unincorporated association other than a partnership or a member of its governing body, and the address is its principal office in the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the proper address of any person is his last known address ... and also"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1259 Documents in electronic form
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17925 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:17926 | (a) section 1258 authorises the giving or sending of a notice, direction or other document by its delivery to a particular person (“the recipient”), and
-- src:17927 | (b) the notice, direction or other document is transmitted to the recipient—
-- src:17928 | (i) by means of an electronic communications network, or
-- src:17929 | (ii) by other means but in a form that requires the use of apparatus by the recipient to render it intelligible.
@ref s 1259(1) Documents in electronic form: when the section applies (src:17925-17929)
GIVEN `section 1258 authorises the giving or sending of the document by its delivery to the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is transmitted to the recipient by means of an electronic communications network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is transmitted to the recipient by other means but in a form that requires the use of apparatus by the recipient to render it intelligible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1259(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF       `section 1258 authorises the giving or sending of the document by its delivery to the recipient`
         AND (`the document is transmitted to the recipient by means of an electronic communications network`
              OR `the document is transmitted to the recipient by other means but in a form that requires the use of apparatus by the recipient to render it intelligible`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where"

-- src:17930 | (2) The transmission has effect for the purposes of this Part as a delivery of the notice, direction or other document to the recipient, but only if the recipient has indicated to the person making the transmission his willingness to receive the notice, direction or other document in the form and manner used.
@ref s 1259(2) Documents in electronic form: effect as delivery (src:17930-17930)
GIVEN `this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recipient has indicated to the person making the transmission his willingness to receive the document in the form and manner used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1259(2) the transmission has effect as a delivery of the document to the recipient` MEANS
    IF NOT `this section applies`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1), "This section applies where"
    ELSE IF `the recipient has indicated to the person making the transmission his willingness to receive the document in the form and manner used`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but only if the recipient has indicated ... his willingness"

-- src:17931 | (3) An indication to a person for the purposes of subsection (2)—
-- src:17932 | (a) must be given to the person in such manner as he may require,
-- src:17933 | (b) may be a general indication or an indication that is limited to notices, directions or other documents of a particular description,
-- src:17934 | (c) must state the address to be used,
-- src:17935 | (d) must be accompanied by such other information as the person requires for the making of the transmission, and
-- src:17936 | (e) may be modified or withdrawn at any time by a notice given to the person in such manner as he may require.
@ref s 1259(3) Documents in electronic form: the indication (src:17931-17936)
GIVEN `the indication is given to the person in such manner as he may require` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indication states the address to be used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indication is accompanied by such other information as the person requires for the making of the transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1259(3) the indication meets the requirements of subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF       `the indication is given to the person in such manner as he may require`
         AND `the indication states the address to be used`
         AND `the indication is accompanied by such other information as the person requires for the making of the transmission`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) must be given ... (c) must state the address to be used, (d) must be accompanied by such other information" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-D)

@ref s 1259(3)(b) Documents in electronic form: a general or limited indication (src:17933-17933)
GIVEN `the indication is a general indication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indication is limited to documents of a particular description` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is of that description` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1259(3)(b) the indication covers the document` MEANS
    IF `the indication is a general indication`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the indication is limited to documents of a particular description` AND `the document is of that description`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an indication that is limited to notices, directions or other documents of a particular description"

@ref s 1259(3)(e) Documents in electronic form: modification or withdrawal (src:17936-17936)
GIVEN `a notice modifying or withdrawing the indication has been given to the person in such manner as he may require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1259(3)(e) the indication has been modified or withdrawn` MEANS
    IF `a notice modifying or withdrawing the indication has been given to the person in such manner as he may require`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be modified or withdrawn at any time by a notice given to the person in such manner as he may require"

-- src:17937 | (4) In this section “electronic communications network” has the same meaning as in the Communications Act 2003 (c. 21).
@ref s 1259(4) Documents in electronic form: "electronic communications network" (src:17937-17937)
GIVEN `the network is an electronic communications network within the meaning of the Communications Act 2003` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1259(4) the network is an electronic communications network` MEANS
    `the network is an electronic communications network within the meaning of the Communications Act 2003`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) whenever the input is NOTHING
